  "body": "## What changed\n`setups_page` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs`) no longer repeats a setup's settings. Removed from the per-setup loop: Part alignment, Lay on a plane, three points, Axes in the plane, Work offset. Removed after the New setup row: the workholding section and the tool list. The no-setup branch (Create first setup + implicit workholding and tool list) is untouched.\n\nType: `feat` (new per-row control, changed page layout), not corrective only.\n\n## What a user sees now\n- **Setups page:** each setup row (name click-to-activate, \"(active)\", the one status line, **Open page**, Delete), the New setup row (Carry stock and WCS over + New setup), Export setup sheets, and a one-line pointer to the setup pages.\n- **Setup<n> page:** unchanged; alignment, plane, points, axes and work offset on Settings, workholding on Fixtures, tool list on Tools.\n- **Way in:** nothing on the Setups page opened a Setup<n> page (the name only activates; the browser's Setup<n> node opens it). Added a small **Open page** button per row: it sets the same `UiTarget::SetupNode(name, Settings)` the browser row does and focuses (activates) the setup via the browser's `focus()` helper, because the Fixtures and Tools pages only edit the active setup. No new command, no new state.\n- `sheet_footer`'s hint is replaced by a truthful pointer; the old line about the Stock/Work offset pages is gone from this page.\n\n## Tests\nNo existing test drove alignment or workholding through the Setups page (all already open `SetupNode`), so none needed re-pointing; the lib suite went from 536 to 538 passed (two new), none removed.\nPinning (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setups_declutter.rs`):\n- `the_setups_page_lists_setups_only_and_each_setup_page_keeps_its_settings`: two setups and a fixture; Setups page has 2 Delete, 2 Open page, New setup, Export, and none of Part alignment / Lay on a plane / Axes in the plane / Work offset / workholding / Tool list; Open page lands on Setup2 and activates it; each Setup<n> page (Settings, Fixtures, Tools) still shows them.\n- `a_document_without_setups_keeps_its_implicit_sections_on_the_setups_page`.\n\nGate: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` (538 ok), clippy -D warnings camcraft-ui, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green.\n\n## Not exercised\nNot seen on screen. The pixel goldens of this page will differ at the next cut (no PNG touched). Diff stays inside `setups_page` to merge trivially with #1090/#1097/#1060/#1100/#706/#770.\n\nChangelog: The Setups page lists setups only (with an Open page button); alignment, work offset, workholding and tool list stay on each setup's own page (#1104)\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1104\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
